The record interval `tau_R` is derived above; it is not discarded merely
because a four-dimensional gauge coefficient is dimensionless. Spatial and
temporal cell scales may cancel only after the exact geometric map is shown.

For an orthogonal physical cell with edge lengths `ell_mu`, volume

```text
V_cell=product_mu ell_mu,
```

and face flux

```text
xi_(mu nu)=ell_mu ell_nu F_(mu nu)+higher-order terms,
```

the tetrad/Hodge-induced positive face metric in the coordinate-flux basis is

```text
<xi,xi>_(2,ell)
  =sum_(mu<nu) [V_cell/(ell_mu^2 ell_nu^2)] xi_(mu nu)^2.
```

Therefore each cell contributes

```text
V_cell sum_(mu<nu) F_(mu nu)^2
```

in the local orthonormal frame. For a general coframe `theta^a=e^a_mu dx^mu`,
the same map is defined by pulling the bivector through
`wedge^2(e^(-1))` and multiplying by `|det e|`. The diagonal formula above
is a mandatory exact check.